      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1372142023">
          <groundspeak:date>2026-07-15T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP183 Wayne [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I came here after an unofficial failure at BCP302 near downtown Drumheller. Those surroundings have changed so much I can’t decide if there’s any chance of still finding it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This one is in a great location and is doing fine, since it’s probably been touched mainly by snakes and geocachers. It does feel like it should be decades older; it’s likely one of the newest manmade objects in the area. Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="687621238">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-20T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="6252216">hunthikers</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP183 Wayne

Hunthikers took a trip E for a change, with the goal to geobike along the 11 Bridges road with the geokids and explore the Drumheller area (a place we have never visited before). The weather was warm and comfortable for biking with no wind to worry about. As a bonus to the caches we found, we were also able to grab a few caps.  This one is tucked into the grass on a little elevated flat area.

{found}

TFTC&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684672350">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP183 - Wayne&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for another day of capping and caching with OBA, this time we went east!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Quite a few people camping nearby!! I love this little valley! So nice and beautiful and quiet!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Cap is in great shape!!! TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
